  "name": "delivery readiness",
  "definition": "A per-criterion projection that keeps requirement, plan, and delivery coverage separate. A criterion is delivered only when it has current immutable evidence and no delivery or transitive dependency blockers; the app is peer-review ready only when every accepted criterion is delivered. Work progress, including done, never counts as proof, and readiness is not an approval verdict.",
